  <project_license>Apache-2.0</project_license>
  <name>ForskScope</name>
  <summary>Compare and merge files and folders, locally</summary>
  <description>
    <p>
      ForskScope is a local-first diff and merge tool. It opens two files
      side by side, highlights every changed line, and lets you apply
      changes from one side to the other one at a time. It also compares
      two folders, recursively, through a two-pane Explorer.
    </p>
    <p>
      Everything runs on your own computer: no account, no upload, no
      telemetry. The one exception is the optional "Check for updates"
      button in the About dialog, which sends a single request to GitHub
      for the latest version number, and only when you click it.
    </p>
    <p>
      ForskScope works as a Git difftool and mergetool, and can be driven
      from a script or an AI agent (the bundled "compare" and "mcp"
      subcommands).
    </p>
  </description>
